{
    "name": "E2E Utils Controls - Each sequential item timeout",
    "description": "Iterates [\"a\",\"b\",\"c\"] with Each in Sequential mode and a 60 s Item Timeout. A Condition lets only items other than 'b' reach Continue Each, so 'b' is never confirmed. Each must give up on 'b' after the Item Timeout, emit 'c' and finish: the Assert on the 'done' port (count = 3) fires only when the loop did not hang. Takes 1-2 minutes by design. Continue Each adds each confirmed item to the Result, so 'done' must carry [\"a\",\"c\"] - the skipped 'b' contributes nothing.",
    "notes": {
        "57f09353-29ab-4429-ac17-f0dbdf5fc3b4": {
            "x": 64,
            "y": 272,
            "width": 672,
            "height": 176,
            "content": "## ⏱ Timing constraint\n\nItem 'b' is filtered out by the Condition on purpose, so it is never confirmed by Continue Each. The loop continues only after the **Item Timeout (60 s, the engine minimum)** plus the timeout job's polling interval. Expect 1-2 minutes of nothing happening between item 'b' and item 'c' - that is the behaviour under test, not a stall. Do not lower the AfterAll timeout below 300 s."
        }
    },
